course: dictionary
lesson: 15565
title: Giving up: the word surrendered
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Surrendered is a verb, the past form of surrender. It tells you something already happened. To surrender means to give up or hand something over. «The soldiers surrendered at dawn.» The soldiers stopped fighting, so surrendered means gave up.
explain: Look at the clues around the word. «She surrendered her ticket at the gate.» Nobody was fighting here, so surrendered means handed over. Try swapping in "gave up" or "handed over" and see which one still makes sense in the sentence.
explain: Sometimes a sad thing is said in a gentler way. At an animal shelter, a pet that its owner has given up may be called a surrendered pet. «The surrendered dog was given a new home.» This is a soft, official way of saying the owner could not keep the dog.
fact: Surrendered is the past form of surrender: surrender, surrenders, surrendered, surrendering.
fact: «Surrendered» means gave up in a fight or war and stopped fighting.
fact: «Surrendered» can also mean handed something over, often because you must, as in «surrendered his passport».
fact: A surrendered pet is one given up by its owner to an animal shelter. This is an official word.
fact: A euphemism is a softer word used in place of a harder one, to make something sound less sad.
exercise: «The army surrendered after three weeks of fighting.» What does surrendered mean? | Won the battle with great pride | Ran away to the hills | Ate a big meal | *Gave up and stopped fighting
exercise: «The guard surrendered his keys at the end of his shift.» What does surrendered mean here? | *Handed them over, because he had to | Lost them on purpose | Made them shine | Bought new ones
exercise: Which word in «The pet was surrendered to the shelter last week» shows it was given up by its owner? | pet | *surrendered | last | shelter
test: «The rebels surrendered when they ran out of food.» Why did they surrender? | They won the castle | *They gave up because they could not keep fighting | They went to sleep | They were given a prize
test: Why might an animal shelter call a pet "surrendered"? | Because the pet had won a prize | Because the pet was lost in the park | *Because its owner gave the pet up to the shelter | Because the pet was very old
exam: Tom says surrendered means won the battle. What does surrendered really mean? | Asked for a drink | Ran a long race | *Gave up and stopped fighting, or handed something over | Won the battle with a loud cheer
